XAIOTEST TITLE 'XAIOTEST - PROVE THE XAIO MACRO SET ASSEMBLES'
         PRINT GEN,DATA
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*  A TRIGGER MODULE FOR THE XAIO MACROS, ON THE PATTERN THAT CLOSED   *
*  M0:  ASSEMBLE THE NEW THING BY ITSELF BEFORE PUTTING IT ANYWHERE   *
*  NEAR A NUCLEUS MODULE, AND PRINT GEN,DATA SO THE EXPANSION AND THE *
*  GENERATED CONSTANTS ARE BOTH VISIBLE IN THE LISTING.               *
*                                                                     *
*  WHAT THIS IS CHECKING IS NOT THAT THE MACROS ARE CORRECT -- ONLY   *
*  EXECUTION SHOWS THAT -- BUT THAT THEY EXPAND, THAT EVERY SYMBOL    *
*  THEY REFERENCE RESOLVES, THAT &SYSNDX KEEPS THE GENERATED LABELS   *
*  UNIQUE ACROSS SEVERAL CALLS IN ONE MODULE, AND THAT THE CHOSEN     *
*  CONDITION-CODE SEQUENCES ARE REAL INSTRUCTIONS.  TWO CC BUGS WERE  *
*  ALREADY FOUND BY READING THEM BACK:  LTR ON A POSITIVE VALUE SETS  *
*  CC2, NOT CC1, AND NOTHING IN THE LTR FAMILY CAN SET CC3 AT ALL.    *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
XAIOTEST CSECT
R0       EQU   0
R1       EQU   1
R2       EQU   2
R3       EQU   3
R4       EQU   4
R5       EQU   5
R6       EQU   6
R7       EQU   7
R8       EQU   8
R9       EQU   9
R10      EQU   10
R11      EQU   11
R12      EQU   12
R13      EQU   13
R14      EQU   14
R15      EQU   15
         USING XAIOTEST,R12
         USING PSA,R0          FOR CAW AND CSW
         SPACE 2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*  THE S/370 IDIOM THIS REPLACES, FROM DMKCKP SEQ 00307000:           *
*                                                                     *
*       TIOSYS   ST    R0,CAW                                         *
*       TIOSYS1  TIO   0(R2)          CLEAR DEVICE                    *
*                BNZ   *-4                                            *
*                SIO   0(R2)          START                           *
*                BNZ   TIOSYS                                         *
*                TIO   0(R2)          TEST                            *
*                BC    6,*-4                                          *
*                CLC   CSW+4(2),=AL1(X'0C',0)                         *
*                                                                     *
*  AND THE SAME THING AFTERWARDS.  NOTE THE BRANCHES ARE UNCHANGED -- *
*  THAT IS THE POINT OF NORMALISING THE CONDITION CODES -- EXCEPT     *
*  THAT *-4 NO LONGER LANDS ON THE TEST, SINCE A MACRO IS LONGER THAN *
*  FOUR BYTES, SO SELF-RELATIVE BRANCHES MUST BECOME LABELS.  THAT IS *
*  A REAL COST OF THIS APPROACH AND IS WORTH SEEING HERE.             *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LA    R2,X'190'      A DEVICE ADDRESS TO TEST WITH
         ST    R0,CAW         THE CALLER STILL SETS THE CAW
TESTCLR  XATIO R2             CLEAR DEVICE
         BNZ   TESTCLR        LOOP WHILE NOT FREE
         XASIO R2             START, CCW ADDRESS FROM THE CAW
         BNZ   TESTCLR        NOT STARTED, GO ROUND AGAIN
TESTWAIT XATIO R2             TEST FOR COMPLETION
         BC    6,TESTWAIT     LOOP IF BUSY OR STATUS STORED
         CLC   CSW+4(2),=AL1(X'0C',0) CHANNEL END WITH DEVICE END ?
         BNE   TESTBAD        NO
         SPACE 1
*  A SECOND SET, TO PROVE &SYSNDX KEEPS THE GENERATED LABELS APART.
         LA    R3,X'00C'      A DIFFERENT DEVICE
         XASIO R3             SECOND DEVICE, SECOND EXPANSION
         XATIO R3
         XAHIO R3             HALT IT
TESTBAD  DS    0H
         BR    R14
         SPACE 2
         XAIOWORK             WORK AREAS AND THE LOOKUP SUBROUTINE
         SPACE 2
         LTORG
         PSA
         COPY  XABLOKS        FOR ORBCCWFM
         END
